{"schema_version":"1.9.2","id":"OESA-2026-4932","published":"2026-11-19T01:43:12Z","modified":"2026-11-19T02:00:16.930416508Z","upstream":["CVE-2026-91150"],"summary":"cockpit security update","details":"Cockpit makes GNU/Linux discoverable. See Linux server in a web browser and perform system tasks with a mouse. It’s easy to start containers, administer storage, configure networks, and inspect logs with this package.\r\n\r\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\nA flaw was found in Cockpit. This vulnerability allows a remote attacker, without prior authentication, to send specially crafted fragmented WebSocket messages. These messages accumulate without a total-size limit, leading to unbounded memory exhaustion and a denial of service in the `cockpit-ws` service.(CVE-2026-91150)","affected":[{"package":{"name":"cockpit","ecosystem":"openEuler:22.03-LTS-SP4","purl":"pkg:rpm/openEuler/cockpit&distro=openEuler-22.03-LTS-SP4"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"178-20.oe2203sp4"}]}],"ecosystem_specific":{"aarch64":["cockpit-178-20.oe2203sp4.aarch64.rpm","cockpit-debuginfo-178-20.oe2203sp4.aarch64.rpm","cockpit-debugsource-178-20.oe2203sp4.aarch64.rpm","cockpit-devel-178-20.oe2203sp4.aarch64.rpm"],"noarch":["cockpit-cockpit-machines-178-20.oe2203sp4.noarch.rpm","cockpit-cockpit-machines-ovirt-178-20.oe2203sp4.noarch.rpm","cockpit-help-178-20.oe2203sp4.noarch.rpm"],"src":["cockpit-178-20.oe2203sp4.src.rpm"],"x86_64":["cockpit-178-20.oe2203sp4.x86_64.rpm","cockpit-debuginfo-178-20.oe2203sp4.x86_64.rpm","cockpit-debugsource-178-20.oe2203sp4.x86_64.rpm","cockpit-devel-178-20.oe2203sp4.x86_64.rpm"]},"database_specific":{"source":"https://repo.openeuler.org/security/data/osv/OESA-2026-4932.json"}}],"references":[{"type":"ADVISORY","url":"https://www.openeuler.org/zh/security/security-bulletins/detail/?id=openEuler-SA-2026-4932"},{"type":"ADVISORY","url":"https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-91150"}],"database_specific":{"severity":"High"},"severity":[{"ty